WEBVTT

00:00.090 --> 00:02.610
-: So, this section is all oriented around installation

00:02.610 --> 00:04.470
and setup, nothing very glamorous,

00:04.470 --> 00:07.020
but a lot of critical content that we'll need

00:07.020 --> 00:08.250
to move forward.

00:08.250 --> 00:09.570
So, the first thing we cover

00:09.570 --> 00:11.820
are the two main ways of using Git,

00:11.820 --> 00:15.210
from the command line and from graphical user interfaces.

00:15.210 --> 00:17.670
That isn't a very important distinction to understand.

00:17.670 --> 00:20.364
We'll be playing around with both throughout the course.

00:20.364 --> 00:22.920
And, then we focus on installing Git.

00:22.920 --> 00:24.750
So, I have separate instructions for Mac

00:24.750 --> 00:26.331
versus Windows users.

00:26.331 --> 00:29.130
That's definitely going to be critical.

00:29.130 --> 00:30.360
I marked it as yellow

00:30.360 --> 00:32.910
just because it can take a little bit of time

00:32.910 --> 00:34.230
if you're on a Windows machine.

00:34.230 --> 00:36.690
It's not hard, you just have to change some settings,

00:36.690 --> 00:38.130
and watch the video, you'll see.

00:38.130 --> 00:40.440
We just click a bunch of times, and hit "next,"

00:40.440 --> 00:42.060
and then hit "next," and then hit "next."

00:42.060 --> 00:43.620
But, obviously, very critical.

00:43.620 --> 00:45.990
We also install an application called GitKraken.

00:45.990 --> 00:48.990
It's a GUI for Gits, it's free.

00:48.990 --> 00:50.340
I guess it's not critical.

00:50.340 --> 00:52.350
You don't have to use it if you wanna use Git,

00:52.350 --> 00:54.900
but I'm gonna put it as important/critical,

00:54.900 --> 00:57.630
because for this course we'll be using this,

00:57.630 --> 01:00.480
but it is not critical to Git, itself.

01:00.480 --> 01:02.760
Configuring your Git name and email, critical,

01:02.760 --> 01:04.680
but also very quick and easy.

01:04.680 --> 01:07.800
And then, the biggest question mark in this section

01:07.800 --> 01:09.810
is the terminal crash course videos.

01:09.810 --> 01:12.507
There are three videos at the end of this section

01:12.507 --> 01:16.380
that are absolutely critical if you have no experience

01:16.380 --> 01:20.130
working with terminal commands, basic Unix commands,

01:20.130 --> 01:23.100
like LS, and CD, and Touch.

01:23.100 --> 01:25.110
So, if you're familiar with those,

01:25.110 --> 01:27.690
you can skip those videos, and they're not critical.

01:27.690 --> 01:30.664
They're not really Git specific at all.

01:30.664 --> 01:32.940
So, if you have experience, you can skip those.

01:32.940 --> 01:37.320
But, if it's all new to you, I 100% would sit through them.

01:37.320 --> 01:38.310
You don't need to take notes,

01:38.310 --> 01:40.110
but practice along with those videos,

01:40.110 --> 01:41.730
they are very important.

01:41.730 --> 01:44.160
If you wanna be able to use Git down the line,

01:44.160 --> 01:46.560
we have to be able to navigate through the terminal.

01:46.560 --> 01:48.300
So, most things in this section are critical,

01:48.300 --> 01:49.650
but no big concepts.

01:49.650 --> 01:50.940
It's just installation,

01:50.940 --> 01:53.670
plus this weird thing at the end with the terminal.

01:53.670 --> 01:56.220
I highly recommend checking that out if you're new.
